WEBVTT

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.930
in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.330
The reading from the Sinaxadium for June 1st, on which we commemorate our righteous

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:17.620
Father Justin of Celizia.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:25.320
Our Holy Father Justin, abbot of Celizia monastery in Valgevo, Western Serbia, was born to

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:34.040
Pius and God-fearing parents, Brota Spiridon, and Protinika Anastasia Popovic, in Vranje,

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:41.480
South Serbia, on the feast of the Annunciation, March 25th, 1894.

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:49.470
Brota means priest, and Protinika means Presbytera.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:55.110
He was born into a priestly family, as seven previous generations of the Popovic's were

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.110
headed by priests.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:04.430
Popovic in Serbian actually means family, or Son, of a priest.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:11.510
At baptism, he was given the name Blagoge, after the feast of the Annunciation.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:17.510
Blagovest means Annunciation, or good news.

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:23.070
Being raised in a pious Christian atmosphere, young Blagoge learned quite early of the

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:29.230
virtuous life in Christ, as dedicated in service to God's Holy Church.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:35.510
As a child, he often visited with his parents the Prohor Pciński monastery, dedicated to

00:01:35.510 --> 00:01:38.590
Saint Prohor, the miracle worker.

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:44.590
He witnessed firsthand the miraculous power of the Lord manifested through Saint Prohor,

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:50.750
as his mother, Anastasia, was healed of a deadly disease by the saint's intercessions,

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:54.950
and Blagoge was still a young boy.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:59.030
Blagoge was an excellent student in elementary school.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:05.150
His greatest love was for the Bible, and the four gospels, in particular.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:11.110
He began serious reading of the Bible at age 14, and throughout the rest of his life he carried

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:18.070
the New Testament on his person, reading faithfully three chapters a day.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:25.070
In 1905, after finishing the fourth grade in Wranje, following the tradition of the Popovic

00:02:25.070 --> 00:02:31.830
family, young Blagoge entered the nine-year program of secular and religious study at the

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:35.470
seminary and faculty of Saint Sava in Belgrade.

00:02:35.470 --> 00:02:41.390
In the early twentieth century, the School of Saint Sava in Belgrade was renowned throughout

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:50.470
the Orthodox world, as a holy place of extremist cynicism, as well as of a high-quality scholarship.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:57.190
Some of the well-known professors were the Rector, Father Domentian, Professor Father

00:02:57.190 --> 00:03:06.390
Dosythios, Later Abyssal, and Athanasios Popovic, and the great ecclesial composer, Stephen

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:14.110
Mokranje, yet one professor stood ahead in shoulders above the rest, the then Hyromunk

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:24.550
Nikolai Velomitevich, Ph.D., Father Nikolai, the single most influential person in his life.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:32.110
From the venerable Nikolai, Blagoge learned of the virtuous ascetic life in Christ, the Lord,

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:38.470
the doctrinal genius of the great fathers of the Church, and of the spiritual and intellectual

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:46.870
effort needed to probe the important philosophical and theological questions of the day.

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:54.510
In the end, both of these two spiritual geniuses possessed a commitment to Christ the Lord,

00:03:54.510 --> 00:04:01.350
which provided them with a truly Orthodox vision of life, which in turn made them the

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:07.950
two greatest voices of the Serbian Orthodox Church in modern times.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:17.150
Both Nikolai and Blagoge, later monk Justin, sought to speak the truth in love to a passing

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:19.390
world.

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:25.470
They sought the answers to the world's most pressing problems in the teachings of the Scriptures

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:30.750
and the fathers of the Church, and especially in the experiences found in the lives of the

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.310
saints.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:41.790
The saints were for them living Bibles, incarnate dogmas, and the true source of Orthodox theology,

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:50.630
experiential knowledge of God, and existential pedagogical truth valid for all times.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:59.470
In 1914, at the age of 20, Blagoge had finished the nine-year program of Saint Savas in Belgrade.

00:04:59.470 --> 00:05:06.710
At this time, he had only one desire in mind that I may dwell in the house of the Lord

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:13.310
all the days of my life, that I may behold the delight of the Lord, and that I may visit

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:16.030
his holy temple.

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:21.110
With this hunger and thirst for righteousness driving him, Blagoge wanted to radically

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:25.390
devote his life to Christ in the monastic vocation.

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:33.550
However, due to the beginning of World War I in 1914 and the declining health of his parents,

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:39.910
Blagoge decided to postpone his entrance into the monastic ranks.

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:46.790
During the early part of World War I, autumn of 1914, Blagoge served as a student nurse,

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:53.230
primarily in South Serbia, Skadar, Nis, Kosovo, etc.

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:59.870
Unfortunately, while in this capacity he contracted typhus during the winter of 1914 and had

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:04.150
to spend over a month in a hospital in Nis.

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:09.070
On January 8th of 1915, he resumed his duties.

00:06:09.070 --> 00:06:14.230
It suits to say that Blagoge and the rest of the aides and nurses, as well as all of the

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:20.270
freedom-loving Serbian Christians in South Serbia, suffered bitterly from the effects of the

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.310
war.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:30.590
On the eve of the feast of St. Nicholas, his Sna Slava, family patron saint, 1915, Blagoge

00:06:30.590 --> 00:06:37.090
returned to Skadar in order to visit metropolitan Dmitrius, who later became the first patriarch

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:42.270
after the patriarchal throne was renewed in 1920.

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:49.710
Blagoge received the monastic tuncher in the church in Skadar, taking the name Justin, after

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:56.910
the great Christian philosopher and martyr for Christ, St. Justin, the philosopher.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:04.070
This name was truly a gift and sign from heaven, for it was as a philosopher and seeker of Christian

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:11.740
truth that the humble monk Justin would later receive glory from God.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:16.660
Shortly after becoming a monk, Justin, along with several other students who received

00:07:16.660 --> 00:07:23.580
the Metropolitan's blessing, traveled to Petrograd, Russia, to begin a year's study

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:26.540
in the orthodox seminary there.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:31.760
It was there the young monk Justin first dedicated himself more fully to orthodoxy and the

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:33.700
monastic way.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:40.660
He learned of the great ascetics of Russia, Anthony and Fildosius of the Caves in Kiev, Seraphim

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:47.780
of Satov, Sergeus of Radhanes, John of Constant and others.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:53.420
Justin fell in love with Russian spirituality and piety, especially that exhibited by the

00:07:53.420 --> 00:07:57.460
common folk of the countryside.

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:03.540
After his year's study and sojourn in Russia, Justin entered by the prompting of his spiritual

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:08.460
father Nikolai, the theological school in Oxford, England.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:17.820
He spent seven semesters at Oxford, November 1916 to May 1919, yet he did not receive a diploma

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:23.940
since his doctoral dissertation entitled The Philosophy and Religion of Dostoevsky was

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:26.340
not accepted.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:33.220
As a result, Justin returned to Belgrade after the war and became a teacher in the seminary

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:35.900
at Katerovak Strem.

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:41.620
At Sremsky Katerovak, Justin renewed the ancient study of the lives of the saints, as being

00:08:41.620 --> 00:08:47.220
a proper theological focus and most important course of study.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:52.060
It was at this time that he received the calling and vision from God to translate into modern

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:58.940
servient the entire lives of the saints of the orthodox church, a feat which to this day

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:03.010
is truly astounding.

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:09.890
In September of 1919, Justin entered the Greek Orthodox School of Theology in Athens, Greece.

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:13.930
He spent two years there to finish his doctoral coursework.

00:09:13.930 --> 00:09:19.690
Just as in Russia, monk Justin traveled throughout the countryside of Greece, especially benefiting

00:09:19.690 --> 00:09:25.970
spiritually from the Greek Orthodox heritage commonly known as the Byzantine legacy.

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:32.730
In 1920, venerable Justin was ordained deacon and began to experience another side of the

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:38.730
church's liturgical life, leadership of the worship services.

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:44.610
As his liturgical and ascetical life increased, Justin matured spiritually and became known

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:49.730
throughout all of Greece as a most pious ascetic.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:55.530
At this time, due to his unceasing prayer to the most sweet Jesus, Justin was granted by

00:09:55.530 --> 00:10:03.030
the grace of the Holy Spirit, the gift of Umilenezhik coupled with tears.

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:10.470
In May of 1921, deacon Justin returned to Sremsky-Karovak and resumed his teaching duties

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:12.630
at the seminary.

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:19.110
He taught on the New Testament, dogmatics, patristics, and the lives of the saints.

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:24.950
Prior to each lesson of the scriptures, he opened with his short prayer.

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:31.950
Almost sweet Lord, by the power of thy Holy Gospel, and through thy apostles teach me and

00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:37.090
announce through me what I am to say.

00:10:37.090 --> 00:10:43.850
One year later, on the feast of the beheading of John the Baptist, in 1922, venerable Justin

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:49.010
was ordained priest by his holiness, Patriarch Dmitrizh.

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:55.290
Throughout the ordination service, Justin was in tears, crying as a newborn babe in the

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:56.890
Lord.

00:10:56.890 --> 00:11:02.330
His humility attracted many, as his disciples grew rapidly in number.

00:11:02.330 --> 00:11:08.530
Not only students, but also many lay people, came to him for confession, counsel, and spiritual

00:11:08.530 --> 00:11:10.050
healing.

00:11:10.050 --> 00:11:16.250
His most beloved disciples were those pious men and women of the Bogomodjak-Bokret, the

00:11:16.250 --> 00:11:23.850
Serbian prayer movement, originally formed and led by the newly consecrated Bishop Nikolai.

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:30.530
The great Bishop Nikolai, as the great apostle of the 20th century, as the new chrysystem

00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:32.970
of all times.

00:11:32.970 --> 00:11:40.850
These two were as Anthony and Athanasius, and Basil and Gregory of Old, two bodies yet

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:42.730
one mind.

00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:48.810
As their love for our Lord Jesus Christ produced much spiritual fruit in the lives of many

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:51.130
zealots.

00:11:51.130 --> 00:11:57.130
Everyone especially enjoyed singing the spiritual songs written by Bishop Nikolai.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:02.050
These ones, written in the vernacular language of the people, were not only quite spiritual

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:07.370
and edifying, but also were didactic and doctrinal in nature.

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:13.610
And it was this praising the Lord in the people's language which inspired Justin to translate

00:12:13.610 --> 00:12:21.290
into modern Serbian, from the original Greek text, the Divine Liturgy of St. John chrysystem.

00:12:21.290 --> 00:12:26.250
Following the scriptural and liturgical tradition of the church, given to the Slavs by the great

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:33.570
evangelical missionaries Cyril and Methodius and their disciples, that is the tradition

00:12:33.570 --> 00:12:39.970
of hearing the word of God and praying in the mother tongues of the people.

00:12:39.970 --> 00:12:47.090
Both Justin and Nikolai were able by the energy of the Holy Spirit to edify and lighten

00:12:47.090 --> 00:12:54.330
and confirm in orthodoxy the pious faithful in their own tongue.

00:12:54.330 --> 00:13:00.530
The zealous Father Justin was also in close contact at this time with two great Russian

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:07.590
orthodox pastors, Metropolitan Anthony Grapovitski, who taught at the seminary in Sremski

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:13.610
Karlova and the exiled Russian bishop John Max Simovic.

00:13:13.610 --> 00:13:19.490
Holy Father John, a man of extreme asceticism, was truly a miracle worker, and is coming

00:13:19.490 --> 00:13:26.570
later to America where he reposed in the Lord in San Francisco, became a blessing and visitation

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:31.330
from the Lord for those God-seekers there.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:37.930
In 1923, Father Justin became the editor of the orthodox journal Christian Life, and in

00:13:37.930 --> 00:13:45.610
this journal appeared his first doctoral dissertation, the philosophy and religion of Dostoevsky,

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:48.730
for which he was persecuted at Oxford.

00:13:48.730 --> 00:13:56.090
Three years later, in 1926, his second doctoral dissertation, the problem of person and knowledge

00:13:56.090 --> 00:14:02.250
in St. Macadios of Egypt, was published in Greek in Athens.

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:08.850
Father Justin was now on his way to establishing himself as a modern father of the church.

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:14.250
For his course on the lives of the saints, Justin began to translate into Serbia in the lives

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:19.610
of the saints from the Greek, Syriac and Slavonic sources, as well as numerous minor

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:28.120
works of the fathers, homilies of John Chrysostom, Macadios and Isaac the Syrian.

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:35.120
He also wrote an exquisite book, The Theory of Knowledge, according to St. Isaac.

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:39.960
Justin's blossoming literary genius amazed everyone.

00:14:39.960 --> 00:14:46.960
In 1931, after a stint as professor in the Theological Academy in Prisren, the brilliant

00:14:46.960 --> 00:14:52.520
father Justin was requested by the Holy Synod in Belgrade to assist Bishop Joseph Svićovich

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:59.320
of Bitala and reorganizing the Church of the Carpatho-Russians in Czechoslovakia.

00:14:59.320 --> 00:15:05.480
This area had been besieged by those espousing unionism.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:10.760
Justin, an established defender of the faith, was a great aid to the reorganization of the

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:14.520
Orthodox Church of Czechoslovakia.

00:15:14.520 --> 00:15:20.680
This experience made him realize a tremendous need of the Serbs to have in their mother tongue

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:25.680
an exact and complete exposition of the Orthodox faith.

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:31.360
As a result, he began writing after his return to Bitala in 1932, his monumental work, The

00:15:31.360 --> 00:15:36.240
Dogmas of the Orthodox Church, in three volumes.

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:42.360
Volume one published in the late 1932 dealt with the sources and method of theology, the nature

00:15:42.360 --> 00:15:48.960
of God and the teaching on the Holy Trinity, creation and divine providence.

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:57.440
This volume was so well received that Dr. Justin was chosen in 1934 as professor of dogmatics

00:15:57.440 --> 00:16:02.800
at the theological faculty of St. Sava in Belgrade.

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:09.880
One year later, this hardworking writer completed the second volume entitled The God-Man and

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:14.640
his work, Christology and Soteriology.

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:20.640
There is no doubt that these two volumes on the third and final volume, ecclesiology,

00:16:20.640 --> 00:16:26.720
teaching on the Church, published later in 1970, are the most complete with his most

00:16:26.720 --> 00:16:33.800
ascetical vision of life, produced for all Christians, a magnificent analysis of the ancient

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:37.120
faith of the Church.

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:42.600
In 1938, Father Justin, along with a number of noted intellectuals of Belgrade, founded the

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:45.800
Serbian Philosophical Society.

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:52.160
Holy Father Justin began at this time to probe the philosophical and world issues of his day.

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:56.280
His penetrating mind was fully displayed in two books.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:17:06.200
The Foundations of Theology, 1939, and Dostoevsky on Europe and Slavism, 1940.

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:11.920
Both of these works dealt with the nature and method of theology and the spirit and vision

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:14.480
of Western civilization.

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:21.160
Father Justin was never fearful of telling the truth concerning the fallen state of humankind,

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:29.180
particularly the follies of Western European religious and secular life.

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:34.860
Father Justin remained in the capacity of professor of dogmatics in Belgrade until the end of World

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:36.700
War II.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:41.700
Within the perspective of the newly established communist and atheistic regime, the likes

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:47.060
of Azele's Christians such as Father Justin, who was now beginning to convert the intellectuals

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:51.460
to faith in Jesus Christ, had no place.

00:17:51.460 --> 00:17:57.620
He alone with several other teachers was ousted from the university system in Belgrade

00:17:57.620 --> 00:18:01.360
and told never to return.

00:18:01.360 --> 00:18:10.820
Thus ended the university teaching career in Belgrade of the great Reverend Dr. Justin Popovic.

00:18:10.820 --> 00:18:17.100
For two years after his exile from Belgrade, the ascetic Justin lived in several monasteries

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:23.340
in Serbia, Kalenik, Ovkar, Sukovov and Ravanitsa.

00:18:23.340 --> 00:18:32.780
And on May 14, 1948, he entered Salija Monastery near the village of Lelik, only a few miles

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:39.060
from the major town of Valjevo, Western Serbia.

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:46.780
Father Justin remained in Salija Monastery until his repose in the Lord on March 25, 1979.

00:18:47.180 --> 00:18:52.220
He became our commander right there and was the spiritual head of the monastery.

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:56.860
Under his guidance, Salija Monastery became a convent.

00:18:56.860 --> 00:19:03.580
A school of iconography renewing the Serbo Byzantine style was also begun there, and a new chapel

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:11.700
dedicated to St. John Chrysostom as well as residential quarters were constructed in 1970.

00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:18.380
Many pious people from all parts of Yugoslavia, Greece, the Balkans and literally all parts

00:19:18.380 --> 00:19:25.620
of the world came to hear him preach and teach the correct faith and life in Christ by the

00:19:25.620 --> 00:19:28.740
energy of the Holy Spirit.

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:34.700
Without a doubt, from the end of World War I until his repose in the Lord, Archimandra

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:40.620
Justin was the pillar of Orthodoxy in his homeland.

00:19:40.620 --> 00:19:47.300
During the time of confinement in Salija Monastery, he accomplished an amazing literary feat.

00:19:47.300 --> 00:19:54.380
He translated and compiled from various sources twelve volumes, one per month, of the lives

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.740
of the saints.

00:19:56.740 --> 00:20:00.140
Father Justin, communed of the Holy Gives daily.

00:20:00.140 --> 00:20:06.460
For the Eucharist, the precious body and blood of our Lord Jesus Christ, was his daily bread

00:20:06.460 --> 00:20:14.500
and the true source of his entire life, work, teaching and existence.

00:20:14.500 --> 00:20:22.220
His words, deed and thoughts exuded a lifestyle reminiscent of the ancient fathers of the church.

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:29.390
Another father of the church walked this earth in the person of St. Justin.

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:34.950
In addition to the lives of the saints, he produced many other writings in Salija, some

00:20:35.030 --> 00:20:40.870
of which are still unpublished, displaying a highly analytical and perceptive mind and

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:42.270
heart.

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:48.870
He actually created a new theological and philosophical language necessary to reach the heart

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:55.550
of the modern human being, and his writings and teachings reflect a genuine and total commitment

00:20:55.550 --> 00:20:58.510
to the Lord Jesus Christ.

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:05.070
A commitment characterized by extreme asceticism, as well as by the contemplative vision of

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:09.510
the divine light of God, the Holy Trinity.

00:21:09.510 --> 00:21:18.190
He was living dogma and a flute of the spirit, reflecting the divine love of God, the Holy Trinity,

00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:22.550
theology was life to St. Justin.

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:29.510
St. Justin fell asleep in the Lord on March 25, 1979, on his birthday, the feast of the

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:31.510
annunciation.

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:34.350
He was 85 years of age.

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:40.030
After his most honorable burial, which was attended by hundreds of pious believers, who came

00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:46.110
from many parts of the world, he was laid to rest facing east, behind the main church

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:48.430
of Salija monastery.

00:21:48.430 --> 00:21:54.470
To this day, Eulogies praising his virtue and love of Christ continue to be heard from

00:21:54.470 --> 00:21:57.750
all parts of the Orthodox world.

00:21:57.750 --> 00:22:03.910
Also miracles have occurred at his gravesite, such as healings, flashes of brilliant and

00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:08.790
divine light from his tomb, as well as many conversions of unbelievers who have either

00:22:08.790 --> 00:22:15.030
read his writings, or have been personally visited by Almighty God through the prayers of

00:22:15.030 --> 00:22:17.430
St. Justin.

00:22:17.430 --> 00:22:22.150
Truly, St. Justin's legacy is a great one.

00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:27.750
Many disciples are now extolling his name and imitating his life by drinking from the inexhaustible

00:22:27.750 --> 00:22:32.750
riches of grace and truth, which he revealed to us.

00:22:32.750 --> 00:22:39.230
O Holy Father Justin, thy sweetness of life refreshes our souls.

00:22:39.230 --> 00:22:45.030
Thy love for truth and desire to live with all the saints is a reminder to us of our own

00:22:45.030 --> 00:22:52.910
calling from God to pursue virtue, that we, most unenlightened and miserable sinners, may

00:22:52.910 --> 00:23:00.190
open our hearts to the knowledge of truth incarnate, the Lord Jesus Christ, to whom belongs

00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:07.550
glory, honor and worship, together with his unoriginate Father, and life-giving Spirit,

00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:14.190
now and ever and unto the ages of ages, amen.

00:23:14.190 --> 00:23:20.470
To the prayers of our Holy Father's, O Lord Jesus Christ our God, of mercy on us and

00:23:20.470 --> 00:23:21.130
save us.
